"Coldharrow's Spire is empty: its augera slipped its chains as the Spire failed and went wild."
"That wild augera still haunts Coldharrow, and lesser minds near it fall into gibbering madness."
"Wild arcana at Coldharrow warps beasts and blurs distance; a lane there can loop back on itself."
"Outside Spire coverage, a person's flare is free of the web; the Fateweavers cannot see there."
"Stavely's harbourmaster takes bribes to let barges past the Army's checks unsearched."
"A Millbeck widow, Hesper Lowe, reads fortunes with glyphed cards; she has a spark of true sight."
